cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this build method, cite it as below and state which preset you used."
title: "Anthropic Serif CJK Rebuild"
abstract: "A source-only, reproducible rebuild of a multilingual serif font. The repository ships no font binaries: the reader supplies a legally obtained proprietary Latin base plus two SIL OFL sources and runs scripts/build_cjk.py locally. Five presets produce cjk (31,724 glyphs), cjk-bold (same coverage, heavier Chinese), multilingual (33,897 glyphs, adds Latin Extended, Greek and Cyrillic), full (47,092 glyphs / 46,963 code points, adds kana, Hangul and CJK symbols) and signature (31,724 glyphs, CJK terminals redrawn from measured Latin design DNA). The output is renamed to Serif CJK Extension by default and preserves all upstream Latin outlines, 19 GSUB features and 2 GPOS features. Repository material is MIT; generated added outlines are SIL OFL 1.1; the upstream Latin outlines are proprietary and not supplied. See LICENSE."
authors:
